---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro"
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
---

<Layout
  title="Mailchimp CSV Too Large | Split import files with FixMyImport"
  description="Fix large Mailchimp CSV imports by splitting them into smaller browser-generated batches."
>
  <main class="w-full px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-14 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-6">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p
            class="text-sm font-medium tracking-[0.14em] text-muted-foreground uppercase"
          >
            Mailchimp guide
          </p>
          <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
            When the CSV is too large, split it before the import does.
          </h1>
          <p class="max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            FixMyImport keeps this simple: remove duplicates first, then split
            the list into smaller files that are easier to upload and retry.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          <div class="border border-border/70 bg-background/70 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">
              Clean before splitting
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-6">
              Trim whitespace and remove empty rows first so each output file
              uses its row budget on real contacts.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-border/70 bg-background/70 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">
              Use selected-column dedupe
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-6">
              Exact-match dedupe on email columns is the fastest way to avoid
              noisy duplicate imports.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-border/70 bg-background/70 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">
              Export predictable batches
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-6">
              Split by size or by rows, keep headers in every file, and download
              the whole batch as a ZIP when needed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <Button asChild>
          <a href="/tools/csv-import-cleaner">Open the CSV Import Cleaner</a>
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
